          "stage2_correction": {
            "pair": "ዮ -> ይ, ኒ -> ነ",
            "reason": "In Classical Ge'ez (Mark 9:18), the verb is የሐቅይ ('he gnashes', from ሐቀየ) and the noun is ስነኒሁ ('his teeth', plural construct ስነኒ- from ስን, translated by ጥርሱንም ያፋጫል on L04). Visually on the page, the final glyph of the first word is 6th-order ይ (with its right-side hook, not a top loop ዮ) and the second letter of ስነኒሁ is 1st-order ነ (two equal legs, whereas the third letter ኒ has the 3rd-order foot)."
